## Context

Filed from the replicator project (`~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator`), no
asker ticket; the author chose this option on 2026-11-25 over (A) reference
notes in replicator's `plans/phase-b.plan` only and (B) schema-level checks in
replicator code.

No skill covers replicating an economics paper by hand with agent help. The
author takes part in the I4R Replication Games in Toulouse on 2026-12-08
(`~/CNRS/missions/actif/2026-12-08 Toulouse Replication Games/`), with a
nominated paper already ticketed in replicator
(`tickets/2026-11-19-imf-wp-26-128-toulouse-pilot.md`). A skill usable by a
session that day is the deadline that matters.

The replicator project (automated agent, Phase B, not started) is the long-run
home of the automated pipeline; this skill is the hands-on, session-driven
counterpart and should not duplicate replicator code.

## Shape (reimagined with the author, 2026-11-25)

Three uses were weighed: assess reproducibility for a reading list, draft a
whole report autonomously, write one interactively. They are not three skills
but three stopping points on one ladder, which the sources already draw: the
CIRED protocol's three child notes (reading note, preliminary assessment,
reproduction report); the ACRe grid, whose L1-L7 depend only on package
contents and L8-L10 on execution; Brodeur's advice to do the mechanical work
before the Games and keep the day for team robustness work.

`/replicate <verb> <paper>`, each verb idempotent and reading only what the
previous verb left in the paper's subproject:

| Verb | Unattended | Writes |
|---|---|---|
| `assess` | yes, batchable | `assessment.json` (grid `acre-i4r-1`, evidence per criterion, run criteria `a_evaluer`), six-row table derived from it, preliminary-assessment Zotero note |
| `reproduce` | yes | run scripts, 3-digit comparison CSVs (discrepancies only), `cra_*`/`crr_*` evidence raising the level |
| `probe` | no: stops at `probe/plan.md` until signed off | robustness scripts and CSVs, one column per alteration |
| `report` | no | I4R template report, reproduction-report Zotero note |

Autonomy is a property of the verb, not a mode. A fully autonomous report is
`assess` + `reproduce` unattended, then a halt at the signed-off `probe` plan:
choosing robustness checks unattended is the cherry-picking rule 4 forbids,
and the unattended pipeline is replicator Phase B's job. The reading-list use
is `assess` alone; `/reading-note`, which already looks for a replication
package, may call it.

**Rule 6 home: a subfolder of replicator** (author's choice, 2026-11-25, over
a dedicated repository or the CIRED project). One subproject per reproduced
paper:

```
replicator/replications/<citekey>/
  manifest.json   DOI, package source, hashes, licence, redistributable?
  fetch.sh        non-redistributable data stays out of git, re-fetched
  assessment.json
  reproduce/  probe/  report/    scripts -> out/*.csv
```

The skill writes there only from a session assigned to replicator (guards:
project files only in the assigned project); the layout is agreed by a
replicator ticket before first use.

**Validation corpus.** The I4R discussion papers give, for hundreds of
papers, the original package and the replicators' own reproducibility table:
a ground truth. replicator's dataset (`replicator dataset fetch --source
i4r`, table `replication_results`) already harvests them. `assess` is checked
row by row against I4R's table; `reproduce` by whether it finds I4R's
discrepancies; `probe` has no ground truth (judgment), scored only for
coverage of the robustness menu. Guards: blind the agent to the I4R report
(pillage 0266 technique 4), include papers published after the model's
training cutoff, keep a held-out split; the corpus skews toward better
packages than a typical reading list. The full held-out benchmark is child
ticket 1554.

